/* The Unsent Museum — interactive literary museum with shared Supabase stories and stars. */
const SCENARIOS=[
 {"id":"friendship","num":"I","title":"The No We Never Said","cn":"The No We Never Said","subtitle":"Sometimes, silence sounds exactly like agreement.","introduction":"There are moments when we want to refuse, yet find ourselves nodding along. Out of politeness, obligation, or fear of disappointing someone, we allow others to mistake our silence for consent. What happens when the words we cannot say are simply “no”?","question":"What do you think I would choose?","story":"At university, our group decided to build a web game for an assignment.\n\nAt first, everything went smoothly. Later, we found that many tools for web coding required payment. Our instructor also had rules about AI-generated coursework, so the extra fees would be difficult to have reimbursed. None of us wanted to spend more money on the project.\n\nAs it happened, I was the only member of our group who had ChatGPT Plus, and it could help us code the web game. That meant almost all the development work would fall to me.\n\nI did not like this arrangement.\n\nI still had my own assignments, lecture slides to study, and other things I had planned to do. Coding would take time and use up a large part of my ChatGPT allowance. When I needed it for my own studies, I might not be able to use it as freely.\n\nWhat bothered me more was that this was a group assignment, yet most of the development work would be mine.\n\nI considered raising an objection.\n\nBut I also knew the others had not subscribed. Asking them to pay for a subscription just for this assignment did not seem entirely reasonable. And we were not strangers. Some of the group members were my friends, and I did not want this issue to affect our relationships.\n\nGrowing up, I seemed to have learned that friends should be understanding toward one another rather than counting every favour.\n\nBesides, I thought carefully about my schedule. Taking on the game development would make me busier, but with enough planning, I believed I could still submit my other assignments before their deadlines.\n\nI understood their difficulties.","silent":["I do not want to disappoint someone who trusts me.","I worry that refusing would seem selfish or unkind.","I feel obliged because this person has helped me before.","I hope the request might disappear if I do not respond clearly.","I am not used to setting boundaries.","I fear that saying no could damage our relationship.","I need more time before I can put my refusal into words."],"speak":["My time and energy deserve respect.","An unclear answer could create false expectations.","I can refuse without rejecting the person.","I would rather be honest now than resentful later.","My circumstances make this commitment unrealistic.","Setting boundaries can protect a relationship.","I want the other person to understand my real wishes."],"research":"Possible research themes: personal boundaries, assertiveness, consent and social obligations.","curatorTrueStory":true,"curatorOutcome":"In fact, I did not voice my objections. I kept my concerns to myself and chose to take on the game development work."},
 {"id":"classroom","num":"II","title":"The Silent Witness","cn":"The Silent Witness","subtitle":"Not every silence concerns only ourselves.","introduction":"We sometimes witness someone else being treated unfairly. We may hesitate to intervene, unsure of what we have seen, afraid of the consequences, or convinced that our words will change nothing. When another person's dignity is at stake, what does it mean to remain silent?","question":"What do you think I chose?","story":"When I was in my first year of high school, a few classmates arranged to go out together one weekend.\n\nThey went to a billiards hall and bought a few cans of alcoholic drinks from a supermarket on the way. The drinks contained around 3% alcohol.\n\nWhile they were at the billiards hall, a colleague of our homeroom teacher happened to see them. The teacher took photographs and sent them to our homeroom teacher.\n\nOur homeroom teacher was very upset about what had happened.\n\nHe told each student involved to write a long reflection. He also contacted their parents one by one, saying that teenagers should not drink alcohol or go to places like billiards halls.\n\nHe said billiards halls could be dangerous because of the people who might spend time there.\n\nBut I did not agree with how he handled the situation.\n\nI knew my classmates were underage, and that they had bought alcoholic drinks. Still, they were spending their own weekend together, and the drinks were not very strong. To me, a billiards hall was simply a place for recreation. Going there did not automatically mean they were in danger.\n\nI felt that the teacher had gone too far.\n\nIn my view, weekends were our own time. Even if a teacher was concerned about students' safety, I did not think this situation needed to be handled in that way.\n\nLater, our homeroom teacher devoted an entire class meeting to the incident.\n\nFor almost the whole period, he talked about the dangers of billiards halls, why minors should not drink, and how students ought to behave.\n\nI thought this was unfair to the rest of us as well. We had not been involved, but we still had to spend a whole class period listening to the warnings.\n\nI considered telling him that I disagreed.\n\nBut he was our homeroom teacher. At school, teachers had far more authority than students, and I was only one student in the class.\n\nWhat made it harder was that he would remain our homeroom teacher for the next two years.\n\nI would still see him every day, attend his classes, hand in my assignments, and speak with him. I did not want a disagreement over this incident to make those ordinary interactions uncomfortable.\n\nI believed his response was unfair. But I also had to think about the two years of high school that still lay ahead of me.","silent":["I worry that speaking up could turn a disagreement into a larger conflict.","I fear that challenging my teacher might affect how he treats me later.","I am not sure I know everything that happened at the billiards hall.","I feel that, as a student, I have little power to question my teacher.","I would rather discuss my disagreement privately than challenge him in front of the class.","I doubt that the teacher would listen to what I have to say.","I want to find a safer way to express a different opinion."],"speak":["My classmates should not have to face unfair criticism alone.","Staying silent might make my teacher think everyone agrees.","I could ask a respectful question without accusing my teacher.","I might regret saying nothing when I believe something is unfair.","I want the class to know that not everyone sees the situation the same way.","Even a small objection might help the teacher reconsider his response.","I believe witnessing unfair treatment gives me a reason to speak."],"research":"Possible research themes: bystander intervention, moral responsibility, social norms and perceived safety.","curatorTrueStory":true,"curatorOutcome":"In fact, I did not challenge my homeroom teacher or voice my disagreement at the class meeting. I chose to remain silent."},
 {"id":"family","num":"III","title":"The Feelings We Never Voiced","cn":"The Feelings We Never Voiced","subtitle":"Some words are hard to say precisely because they matter.","introduction":"A thank-you left unspoken. An apology put off until tomorrow. Affection we hope someone will understand without hearing it. Sometimes we keep our feelings to ourselves, believing there will always be another chance. But what if that moment never returns?","question":"What do you think I chose?","story":"From the day I was born, my grandmother was always there.\n\nShe taught me to read and draw, and she taught me some of the first things I learned about how to live. When I was little, she took me to school and picked me up every day. Much of what I first understood about the world came from her. When I look back on my childhood, she is there in almost every important memory.\n\nI love her very much.\n\nBut I have rarely been able to say those words directly.\n\nI do not know whether this has something to do with the culture in which I grew up. In my experience, saying 'I love you' plainly has always felt embarrassing. Speaking my sincerest feelings aloud is almost like taking the softest part of my heart and laying it bare before another person.\n\nI do not know quite how to face that feeling.\n\nWhen I was younger, I sometimes argued with my grandmother over small things, especially during my rebellious years. Even when I knew I had done something wrong, it could still be difficult to say 'I'm sorry.' Admitting a mistake, like expressing love, seemed to require me to cross some barrier I could hardly describe.\n\nLater, my grandmother was preparing to return to her hometown in Northeast China.\n\nBefore she left, memories kept coming back to me: all the days she had spent beside me since I was small, everything she had taught me, and even our arguments.\n\nI did not want her to go.\n\nI wanted to tell her how much I loved her. I wanted to tell her how much she meant to me. Part of me even wanted to ask her to stay.\n\nAll the words I usually struggled to say kept coming into my mind at that moment.\n\nAnd she was about to leave.\n\nThere was still so much I wanted to tell her.","silent":["I expect they already know how I feel.","I am uncomfortable showing strong emotion aloud.","I fear becoming vulnerable or embarrassed.","I cannot find words that seem adequate.","I believe another opportunity will come.","I worry the other person may not welcome this conversation.","I prefer expressing my feelings through actions."],"speak":["They deserve to hear how much they matter to me.","I might not get another opportunity.","Sincere words need not be perfectly phrased.","I want to prevent a future regret.","A small expression of gratitude could mean a great deal.","Being vulnerable may deepen our connection.","I would rather share my feelings than leave them to guess."],"research":"Possible research themes: emotional expression, gratitude, attachment and missed opportunities.","curatorTrueStory":true,"curatorOutcome":"In the end, I did not say those words aloud. As we said goodbye, my grandmother and I simply held each other tightly. We both cried, but neither of us said anything. Later, she returned to her hometown in Northeast China."},
 {"id":"before-sending","num":"IV","title":"Before Sending","cn":"Before Sending","subtitle":"Not everything written is meant to be delivered.","introduction":"A letter folded into a drawer. An email left in drafts. A message written, reread, and quietly deleted. Here, the words have already found their form, yet stop just before reaching another person. Why do we sometimes keep what we have finally managed to say?","question":"What do you think I chose?","story":"When I was in secondary school, I fell for a boy.\n\nWe were already friends. I could talk to him, spend time with him, and slowly get to know him better.\n\nBut I kept worrying that, if he found out how I felt, things between us might change. He might feel awkward, start avoiding me, or stop speaking to me the way he used to.\n\nI did not want that.\n\nI wanted us to go on being ordinary friends and to feel comfortable around each other at school. I still wanted chances to observe him and discover things I did not yet know about him.\n\nThere were feelings I could never quite tell him directly.\n\nSo I wrote them down.","silent":["I am afraid he might distance himself from me if he finds out.","I want us to stay friends as we are.","I treasure the chance to talk and spend time with him naturally.","I do not want to make him uncomfortable because of my feelings.","I still want to observe him and get to know him better.","Even without saying anything, liking him quietly makes me happy.","I do not know how he would respond, and I do not want to risk changing what we have."],"speak":["I do not want to keep hiding my feelings.","I hope he might have a chance to know how I feel.","I want to find out how he would respond.","I do not want to regret never expressing myself.","I believe sharing my feelings does not necessarily ruin a friendship.","I want to leave a real record of these feelings.","It is easier for me to express my feelings in writing than face to face."],"research":"Possible research themes: letter writing, mediated communication, self-censorship and message revision.","curatorTrueStory":true,"originalDraft":"Somewhere in all this confusion, I think I might have fallen for someone.\n\nBecause whenever I see him, my mood is like a bottle of sparkling water just opened: fresh, sweet bubbles bursting everywhere.\n\nJust thinking of him makes me smile a little, quietly, and my heart feels sweet.\n\nI want to imitate him, observe him, discover more about him. Without realizing it, I want to be closer.\n\nHe is a reserved person who doesn't speak much, and I don't want to bother him.\n\nSo I only watch him from a distance, gently and quietly.\n\nCompared with before, there is now another figure in my life. I think of him often, and he comes to meet me in my dreams.\n\nBut perhaps that is all it can be, all it should be. Maybe it is best this way.\n\nHe is so wonderful and so gentle, but I don't know how to face someone who seems so perfect to me.\n\nPerhaps I should just keep liking him quietly, until this feeling slowly fades.\n\nThen he will always remain that perfect figure in my mind.","originalDraftLabel":"Words left in my drafts","curatorOriginalFootnote":"This scene comes from the curator’s own experience. The draft was written during secondary school. The Simplified Chinese edition reproduces the original wording, punctuation, and paragraph breaks; English and Traditional Chinese are translations.","curatorOutcome":"In fact, I did not publish those words at the time.","curatorOutcomeQuote":"Those words had stayed in my drafts for more than three years. I never dared to press the publish button, yet I treasured them too much to delete them.","curatorPostscriptLabel":"The rest of the original account","curatorPostscript":"All right. I still like you. Today is the day the college entrance exams are coming to an end.\n\nThree years are over. We are going to say goodbye, yet I can still pick out your quiet figure at a glance in the middle of a crowd. We are not taking our exams at the same venue, but luckily, fate placed our schools right next to each other. So close, so close.\n\nAs I walked to my exam, missing you, I looked up and saw you. I watched you enter the exam room. Your tall, straight figure—even without my glasses, I was certain. Absolutely certain.\n\nAll right. I still have my own road to follow. But if there is a chance, if I never meet anyone better than you, then please, let us meet again.\n\nUntil then, stay quietly in my heart, a secret no one knows but me.","curatorPostscriptFootnote":"These paragraphs were written by the curator later, looking back at the same feelings and the end of secondary school. The Simplified Chinese edition retains the original text; English and Traditional Chinese are translations.","curatorAfterwordLabel":"Curatorial note","curatorAfterword":"The curator later chose to publish the piece anonymously in this museum’s public story archive. Publishing the article did not mean confessing those feelings to the boy. The words that were not sent to him and the draft kept for years are two different parts of the same exhibit.","curatorFullStoryLabel":"Read the full published story","curatorFullStoryId":"b22cf251-7d8f-4dcb-b223-0876cdac90ee"}
];

/* Museum-wide language selection. Historical texts are locally authored;
   published visitor stories remain in the language their authors chose. */
const MUSEUM_LANGUAGE_KEY='unsent-museum-language';
let museumLang=(()=>{
 try{const x=localStorage.getItem(MUSEUM_LANGUAGE_KEY);return ['en','zh-Hans','zh-Hant'].includes(x)?x:'en'}catch{return 'en'}
})();
let museumTWConverter=null;
function museumConvert(text){
 if(museumLang!=='zh-Hant')return String(text??'');
 try{if(!museumTWConverter&&window.OpenCC?.Converter)museumTWConverter=window.OpenCC.Converter({from:'cn',to:'hk'});return museumTWConverter?museumTWConverter(String(text??'')).replace(/登錄/g,'登入').replace(/反饋/g,'回饋').replace(/賬户|帳户|賬戶/g,'帳戶').replace(/數據庫/g,'資料庫').replace(/信息/g,'資訊').replace(/電子郵箱|郵箱/g,'電郵地址').replace(/鏈接/g,'連結').replace(/默認/g,'預設'):String(text??'')}
 catch(e){return String(text??'')}
}
function museumZh(text){return museumLang==='en'?String(text??''):museumConvert(window.MUSEUM_I18N?.zh?.[String(text??'')]??String(text??''))}
function museumConfirm(message){return window.confirm(museumZh(message));}
function museumDisplaySystemMessage(value){
 const msg=String(value??'');if(museumLang==='en'||!msg)return msg;
 const dict=window.MUSEUM_I18N?.zh||{};
 if(dict[msg])return museumConvert(dict[msg]);
 if(/invalid login|invalid credentials|invalid email or password/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('邮箱或密码不正确，请核对后重试。');
 if(/email not confirmed|email confirmation/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('请先通过邮件完成账户验证。');
 if(/already registered|user already exists/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('这个邮箱似乎已注册，请尝试登录。');
 if(/rate limit|too many requests/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('尝试次数较多，请稍后再试。');
 if(/password.*(?:weak|short|character)|at least.*character/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('请设置符合要求的密码后重试。');
 if(/send reset link|reset password/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('密码重设邮件未能发送，请检查邮箱地址或稍后再试。');
 if(/restore.*(?:session|login)|recover.*session/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('暂时无法恢复登录状态，请重新登录。');
 if(/network|fetch|timeout|failed to load|connection/i.test(msg))return museumConvert('网络或云端连接暂时不可用，请稍后再试。');
 if(/[A-Za-z]{3}/.test(msg))return museumConvert('操作暂时未能完成，请检查填写的信息后重试。');
 return museumConvert(msg);
}

window.museumLangPublic=()=>museumLang;
window.museumConvertPublic=museumConvert;
function museumLangControl(){
 const isZh=museumLang!=='en';
 const label=isZh?'界面语言':'Language';
 const languageName=isZh?'界面语言':'Website language';
 const english=isZh?'英语':'English';
 const traditional=isZh?'繁体中文':'Traditional Chinese';
 const simplified=isZh?'简体中文':'Simplified Chinese';
 return '<div class="museum-language-switch"><label for="museum-language">'+label+'</label><select id="museum-language" aria-label="'+languageName+'">'+
  '<option value="en"'+(museumLang==='en'?' selected':'')+'>'+english+'</option>'+
  '<option value="zh-Hant"'+(museumLang==='zh-Hant'?' selected':'')+'>'+traditional+'</option>'+
  '<option value="zh-Hans"'+(museumLang==='zh-Hans'?' selected':'')+'>'+simplified+'</option>'+
 '</select></div>';
}
function museumHistoryLocalized(essay,id){
 if(!essay||museumLang==='en')return essay;
 const x=window.MUSEUM_HISTORY_ZH?.[id];
 if(!x)return essay;
 const tr=value=>museumConvert(value);
 const label=window.MUSEUM_HISTORY_LABELS?.[id]||{};
 const story=x.story.map(tr);
 const analysis=[
  [tr('历史背景与社会环境'),tr(x.setting)],
  [tr('沉默究竟发生在哪里？由谁决定？'),tr(x.act)],
  [tr('为什么选择保留，或为什么被迫停止？'),tr(x.cause)],
  [tr('证据能证明到什么程度？'),tr(x.proof)],
  [tr('沉默之后发生了什么？'),tr(x.after)]
 ];
 const old=essay.moment||{};
 return {...essay,title:tr(x.title),subtitle:tr(x.subtitle),period:tr(label.period||essay.period),readingTime:tr('完整中文故事'),story,analysis,question:tr(x.question),
  images:(essay.images||[]).map(pic=>({...pic,caption:museumZh(pic.caption),kind:museumZh(pic.kind),credit:pic.credit})),
  sources:essay.sources||[],
  object:{...(essay.object||{}),name:tr(label.object||x.title),kind:tr(label.kind||'历史文献'),evidence:tr(x.proof)},
  moment:{...old,addressed:tr('请结合上方历史故事与原始资料判断。'),intended:tr(x.act),withheld:tr(x.act),why:tr(x.cause),certainty:tr(x.proof)},
  note:tr('本展品中文版依据同一批历史资料重新组织叙述，并非逐字翻译，篇幅与英文稿可能不同。历史事件与主观动机分别呈现；如需核查，请使用下方的原始资料链接。'),
  tags:(essay.tags||[]).map(v=>tr(window.MUSEUM_I18N?.zh?.[v]||v))};
}
function museumTranslateInterfaceValue(value,dict){
 const original=String(value??''),key=original.trim();
 if(museumLang==='en')return original;
 if(!key)return original;
 let translation=dict[key];
 if(!translation){
  const numerals={I:'一',II:'二',III:'三',IV:'四',V:'五',VI:'六',VII:'七',VIII:'八',IX:'九',X:'十'};
  const gallery=n=>'第'+(numerals[n]||n)+'展厅';
  const dynamic=[
   [/^Shared museum database · ([0-9]+) visitor response\(s\)$/,(_,n)=>'共享博物馆数据库 · '+n+' 份访客回答'],
   [/^([0-9]+) shared answers returned$/,(_,n)=>'已读取 '+n+' 份共享回答'],
   [/^([0-9]+) stars with opted-in public names$/,(_,n)=>n+' 颗星星选择了公开署名'],
   [/^([0-9]+) public stories returned$/,(_,n)=>'已读取 '+n+' 篇公开故事'],
   [/^([0-9]+) own stories accessible$/,(_,n)=>'可访问自己的 '+n+' 篇故事'],
   [/^([0-9]+) published stor(?:y|ies)$/,(_,n)=>n+' 篇已发布的故事'],
   [/^(.+)\.$/,(_,label)=>dict[label]?dict[label]+'。':label+'.'],
   [/^([0-9]+)\s+response\(s\)\s*·.*/i,(_,n)=>n+' 份回答 · 可多选，因此比例合计可能超过百分之百。'],
   [/^RESEARCH\s*·\s*GALLERY\s+([IVX0-9]+)/i,(_,n)=>'研究资料 · '+gallery(n)],
   [/^GALLERY\s+([IVX0-9]+)/i,(_,n)=>gallery(n)],
   [/^Gallery\s+([IVX0-9]+)/i,(_,n)=>gallery(n)],
   [/^([0-9]+)\s+responses?\s*·\s*Multiple choice.*/i,(_,n)=>n+' 份回答 · 可多选，因此比例合计可能超过百分之百。'],
   [/^([0-9]+)\s+reason stars?\s*·\s*([0-9]+)\s+answers?/i,(_,n,m)=>n+' 颗理由星辰 · '+m+' 份回答'],
   [/^([0-9]+)\s+local responses?/i,(_,n)=>n+' 份本地回答'],
   [/^([0-9]+)\s+accounts? in this wing/i,(_,n)=>'本展厅共有 '+n+' 份档案'],
   [/^([0-9]+)\s+(?:stories|responses|stars|reasons|records)\b/i,(_,n)=>n+' 份记录'],
   [/^Blue\s*·\s*Silence/i,()=> '蓝色 · 沉默'],
   [/^Gold\s*·\s*Speak up/i,()=> '金色 · 开口'],
   [/^Could not load (?:public )?(?:stories|star data):/i,()=> '暂时无法载入公开资料：'],
   [/^Cloud (?:backup|save) failed:/i,()=> '云端保存失败：']
  ];
  for(const [re,fn] of dynamic){if(re.test(key)){translation=key.replace(re,fn);break;}}
 }
 if(!translation)return museumConvert(original);
 return original.replace(key,museumConvert(translation));
}
function museumLocalizeText(root){
 if(museumLang==='en'||!root)return;
 const dict=window.MUSEUM_I18N?.zh||{};
 const changed=[];
 const walker=document.createTreeWalker(root,NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);
 let node;
 while((node=walker.nextNode())){
  const parent=node.parentElement;
  if(!parent||parent.closest('script,style,textarea,.archive-prose,.public-story-body,.story-reader-prose,[data-visitor-story],[data-original-language],code,pre'))continue;
  const raw=node.nodeValue,trim=raw.trim();if(!trim)continue;
  const translated=museumTranslateInterfaceValue(raw,dict);
  if(translated!==raw)changed.push([node,translated]);
 }
 changed.forEach(([node,value])=>{node.nodeValue=value});
 for(const attr of ['placeholder','aria-label','title','alt']){
  root.querySelectorAll('['+attr+']').forEach(el=>{
   if(el.closest('[data-visitor-story],[data-original-language]'))return;
   const old=el.getAttribute(attr);
   const newValue=museumTranslateInterfaceValue(old,dict);
   if(newValue!==old)el.setAttribute(attr,newValue);
  });
 }
}
let museumI18nObserver=null;
function museumObserveLocalizedUpdates(root){
 if(museumI18nObserver)museumI18nObserver.disconnect();
 if(museumLang==='en'||!root||typeof MutationObserver==='undefined')return;
 museumI18nObserver=new MutationObserver(records=>{
   const roots=new Set();
   for(const record of records){
    if(record.type==='characterData')roots.add(record.target.parentElement);
    else for(const child of record.addedNodes){if(child.nodeType===1)roots.add(child);else if(child.nodeType===3)roots.add(record.target);}
   }
   museumI18nObserver.disconnect();
   for(const el of roots)if(el&&root.contains(el)&&!el.closest('[data-visitor-story],[data-original-language]'))museumLocalizeText(el);
   museumI18nObserver.observe(root,{childList:true,characterData:true,subtree:true});
 });
 museumI18nObserver.observe(root,{childList:true,characterData:true,subtree:true});
}
function museumBindLanguage(){
 const el=document.getElementById('museum-language');if(!el)return;
 el.value=museumLang;
 el.addEventListener('change',()=>{
  const v=el.value;if(!['en','zh-Hant','zh-Hans'].includes(v))return;
  // A display-language change must not discard an unfinished form.
  const fields=[...document.querySelectorAll('#app form input[id],#app form textarea[id],#app form select[id]')].map(x=>({id:x.id,value:x.value,checked:x.checked}));
  const search=document.getElementById('history-search')?.value;
  const activeTab=document.querySelector('[data-silence-tab][aria-pressed="true"]')?.dataset.silenceTab;
  museumLang=v;try{localStorage.setItem(MUSEUM_LANGUAGE_KEY,v)}catch{}
  document.documentElement.lang=v;render(false);
  for(const field of fields){const target=document.getElementById(field.id);if(target){target.value=field.value;if('checked' in target)target.checked=field.checked;}}
  if(activeTab)document.querySelector('[data-silence-tab="'+activeTab+'"]')?.click();
  if(search){const target=document.getElementById('history-search');if(target){target.value=search;target.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'));}}
 });
}

const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);
const esc=x=>String(x??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const KEY='unsent-museum-prototype-v1';
let db;try{db=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY))||{answers:[],stories:[]}}catch{db={answers:[],stories:[]}}
// Preserve only the newest answer for each scenario in this browser.
// Earlier prototype versions allowed repeated answers, so normalize old local data too.
if(!Array.isArray(db.answers))db.answers=[];
if(!Array.isArray(db.stories))db.stories=[];
function dedupeAnswers(){const seen=new Set();db.answers=db.answers.slice().reverse().filter(a=>{if(!a||!a.scenario||seen.has(a.scenario))return false;seen.add(a.scenario);return true}).reverse()}
dedupeAnswers();
const save=()=>{dedupeAnswers();localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(db))};
let flow={scenario:null,step:0,decision:'',reasons:[],other:'',otherConsent:false,otherLanguage:'auto',share:'',title:'',storyCategory:null,story:'',why:'',consent:false,exhibit:false,starMode:'',starName:'',submitted:false};

